{
  "id": "https://geo-carto.github.io/vocabularios/file-type/arcinfo_cov",
  "type": "Concept",
  "prefLabel": {
    "en": "ArcInfo coverage",
    "es": "ArcInfo coverage"
  },
  "altLabel": {
    "en": [
      "ESRI ArcInfo Coverage"
    ],
    "es": [
      "ESRI ArcInfo Coverage"
    ]
  },
  "definition": {
    "en": "An ESRI ArcInfo coverage is a georelational data model that stores vector data – it contains both the spatial (location) and attribute (descriptive) data for geographic features. Coverages use a set of feature classes to represent geographic features. Each feature class stores a set of points, lines (arcs), polygons, or annotation (text). Coverages can have topology, which determines the relationships between features. A coverage is stored as a directory within which each feature class is stored as a set of files.",
    "es": "Una cobertura ESRI ArcInfo es un modelo de datos georrelacional que almacena datos vectoriales – contiene tanto los datos espaciales (ubicación) como los datos de atributos (descriptivos) para las características geográficas. Las coberturas utilizan un conjunto de clases de características para representar características geográficas. Una cobertura se almacena como un directorio dentro del cual cada clase de característica se almacena como un conjunto de archivos."
  },
  "notation": [
    "multipart/mixed"
  ],
